# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored) for `wrangler dev`. LOCAL dev secrets only.
# The platform config endpoint is public (no secrets required).

# ── THE MONEY RAIL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [pipeline 5]M-1/M-12 · [ADR 004]. POST /v1/money/paddle verifies an HMAC-SHA256
# over the raw body with Paddle's PER-DESTINATION notification secret.
#
# 🔴 OWNER-GATED. This value can only be generated in the Paddle seller console,
# which requires the seller account — OWNER_QUEUE A-1, PENDING. Until it exists
# the route answers 503 and CI PRINTS the gap rather than failing the build.
#
# Generate: Paddle dashboard -> Developer tools -> Notifications -> your
# destination -> the secret key. It begins `pdl_ntfset_`.
# Deploy: `wrangler secret put PADDLE_NOTIFICATION_SECRET` — NEVER as a var in
# wrangler.jsonc, and never committed anywhere (scan-secrets.mjs refuses it).
PADDLE_NOTIFICATION_SECRET=

# ── THE CHECKOUT CREDENTIAL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [ADR 044] · `src/routes/checkout.ts`. POST /v1/checkout creates a Paddle
# transaction with this key as a bearer token. WITHOUT IT A LOCAL CHECKOUT CANNOT
# START: the route refuses with 503 `checkout_not_configured` and logs
# `PADDLE_API_KEY is not set`.
#
# 🔴 IT WAS MISSING FROM THIS FILE UNTIL 2026-08-25 AND THAT WAS A SILENT TRAP.
# The route read the value by name through a cast, so `tsc` never saw the string
# and an env sweep over src/ (19 `env.[A-Z_]+` names) did not list it either — a
# developer following this file verbatim got a Worker whose checkout refused with
# no hint the value had ever been documented anywhere. It is a declared binding
# now (`Env.PADDLE_API_KEY` in src/types.ts), so the name is discoverable from
# the type, and deleting it there fails `npm run typecheck`.
#
# 🔴 OWNER-GATED, the same gate as the secret above. The key is generated in the
# Paddle seller console (OWNER_QUEUE A-1, PENDING) under Developer tools ->
# Authentication. The deployed value is the vault's `PADDLE_API_KEY_LIVE`, and
# the vault QUOTES its values — strip the quotes before pasting or the header
# goes out as `Bearer "…"` and reads exactly like a revoked token.
#
# 🔴 THE PREFIX MUST MATCH MONEY_ENVIRONMENT BELOW. `pdl_live_apikey_` for
# `live`, `pdl_sdbx_apikey_` for `sandbox`; checkout.ts compares the prefix and
# refuses rather than creating a transaction in the other money world ([5]M-12).
# So a local run set to `sandbox` needs the SANDBOX key, not the live one.
# Deploy: `wrangler secret put PADDLE_API_KEY` — NEVER as a var in
# wrangler.jsonc, and never committed (.gitleaks.toml carries both prefixes).
PADDLE_API_KEY=

# Which money world THIS local run is. Exactly `live` or `sandbox`. The deployed
# value lives in wrangler.jsonc `vars` and is `live`; a local run against Paddle's
# sandbox destination sets `sandbox` HERE so a sandbox notification can never be
# written with a live provider_environment.
MONEY_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
